# ============================================================================
#  Fiduciary — .gitignore
#  Goal: NEVER commit secrets or real personal/financial data. Review the
#  SHARING-CHECKLIST.md before your first push.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Secrets & credentials (NEVER commit) ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.demo.example
secrets.env
*.secret
*.key
*.pem

# ---- mcpo / MCP server config (holds URLs, tokens) ----
mcpo/config.json
mcpo/data/
**/config.json
!**/config.json.example
!mcpo/config.json.example

# ---- mcpo secrets bridge (2026-07-24) — portfolio-api-written, holds real Monarch/Tavily creds ----
mcpo-secrets/mcpo.env
!mcpo-secrets/mcpo.env.example

# ---- REAL personal / financial data (Monarch dumps, diagnostics) ----
monarch-*-sample.json
*-sample.json
diag/
holdings.csv

# ---- Logs & diagnostic dumps (can contain PII / tokens — never commit) ----
audit/
*.log
*.tmp
# SEC-1 security event log (2026-07-24) — holds IPs, usernames, encrypted config-change detail
audit.db
audit.jsonl
**/audit.db
**/audit.jsonl

# ---- portfolio-api runtime state (regenerated at runtime; user-specific) ----
data/
**/data/
analysis.json
paper.json
discovery.json
opportunities.json
fees_liquidity.json
scanner.json
retirement.json
accounts.json
settings.json
secrets.json
prompts.json
knowledge_index.json

# ---- Knowledge RAG folder — your own reference docs (may be personal, e.g. your IPS) ----
knowledge/*
!knowledge/README.md
# committed, NON-personal reference docs (estate/QSBS/parameter snapshots) ship with the repo:
!knowledge/reference/
!knowledge/reference/*.md
chat.db

# ---- Internal dev/planning artifacts & real personal data — do NOT share with collaborators ----
# These are working notes/reviews, not user-facing docs, and several embedded real financial
# figures/account names. Untracked 2026-07-22 (were committed earlier by mistake). The whole docs/
# folder is internal R&D EXCEPT DEPENDENCIES.md (a plain, non-personal dependency list linked from
# INSTALL.md). See SHARING-CHECKLIST.md section 4.
# 2026-07-24: the 2026-07-22 pass only untracked these AT THE TIP (git rm --cached) — none of them
# were ever actually scrubbed from HISTORY despite section 4 saying so, and four more
# internal-planning docs were added and committed in the days since (same mistake, again). ALL of
# them — old and new — need a real git-filter-repo pass; see SHARING-CHECKLIST.md section 4 for
# the command block.
RESUME-TRACKER.md
MEMORY-HANDOFF-FROM-LOCAL-AI.md
MIGRATION.md
AWS-DEPLOYMENT-PLAN.md
AWS-HOSTING-GUIDE.md
AWS-DEMO-HOSTING-GUIDE.md
portfolio-api-demo-task.json
CLOUD-PORTABILITY-ROADMAP.md
DISTRIBUTION-MONETIZATION-RESEARCH.md
LOCAL-HOSTING-HARDENING-PLAN.md
SECURITY-CONTROLS-GAP-ANALYSIS.md
DEMO-SITE-BUILD-PLAN.md
POSITIONING-BRIEF.md
docs/*
!docs/DEPENDENCIES.md

# ---- Security/GRC demo evidence (2026-07-25, REVERSED 2026-07-26 — all tracked now) ----
# `compliance/` holds GRC documentation (risk register, ISO 27001 Annex A SoA, IR runbook,
# ROPA/DPIA, the machine-readable controls.json + its generator) alongside the always-tracked
# privacy notice / retention schedule. 2026-07-25's call was to keep only the latter two tracked,
# reasoning that the rest was GRC-audience-only and shouldn't ride along in a potentially public
# repo. Jason's REVERSED call (2026-07-26): having actually used this deployment, the IR runbook
# especially is genuinely useful to any user running their own copy (a normal household admin
# benefits from knowing "what do I do if something looks wrong" as much as a GRC reviewer does) —
# there's no real case for withholding any of these seven files from someone running their own
# instance. All of `compliance/` is tracked now; nothing in it is sensitive (no real personal/
# financial data — see PRIVACY-NOTICE.md's own scope statement).
# NOTE, now moot for these specific files: they were briefly committed in 654c823 (2026-07-25) then
# untracked, so they existed in history either way — re-tracking them going forward makes that
# transitional history irrelevant (the content is intentionally public again). This does NOT
# resolve the SEPARATE, still-open history-scrub debt for the genuinely-internal docs listed above
# (RESUME-TRACKER.md, POSITIONING-BRIEF.md, SECURITY-CONTROLS-GAP-ANALYSIS.md, etc.) — those still
# need the git-filter-repo pass in SHARING-CHECKLIST.md section 4 before this repo goes public.

# ---- Local backups / scratch ----
*.known-good
*.known-good/
*.bak
*~
_synctest*
**/_synctest*

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---- OS / editor cruft ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- Terraform (infra/terraform, 2026-10-16) ----
# State can hold ARNs/IDs and anything sensitive that slips in; remote state lives in S3.
# .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed (pins provider checksums).
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
infra/terraform/backend.hcl
# Read-only live-config dumps from scripts/aws-demo/export-live-config.sh (account IDs, ARNs, IPs)
infra/terraform/.live-snapshot/
# NOTE: demo-env/waf.auto.tfvars.json is intentionally NOT ignored -- public scanner CIDRs + the
# geo allow-list are the WAF's source of truth and need to be in the repo for plan/CI.
